# A1: the AUDITED eight-seat 262k attach of the one-launch SDPA on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-sdpamulti-audit (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-sdpamulti plus QWEN_FAST_TP4_SDPA_AUDIT=1: every attention layer runs the per-user launches AND the multi launch on
# the same inputs in one trace, and a device kernel compares the two block outputs word for word). Never attached on hardware. READ in this order and stop at the first failure: (1) admission passed at capacity 262144,
# the reservation installed with the pool the profile states, extent block engaged blocks=2; (2) the ENGAGED line of EACH block: '[PINDIAG] tp4 sdpa engaged config=multi ... users=4 flags=0x21 cores_per_entry=16 active_cores=64 audit=1' (an attach refusal
# names the shape or the flag: a finding), and the call line '[PINDIAG] tp4 sdpa multi call' (built and never called proves nothing); (3) the audit: at least one '[PINDIAG] tp4 sdpa audit <n> exact=True users=4 layers=16 chips=4 words=<w> live=<l>' per block
# per verify round and ZERO 'audit MISMATCH' or exact=False lines (c2_smoke_check.sdpa_multi_problems fails the arm on either; a mismatch line names the layer and the words that differ); (4) the factory's own line in the native log when it is captured:
# '[QWEN-SDPA] flags=0x21 B=4 PNHt=3 kv_share=false scratch_slots=4' (scratch_slots=4 is the proof of 16 cores per entry: a graft that is mounted is not necessarily the one executed); (5) every answer's hash equal to solo and, per request, the accepted
# tokens and verify rounds equal to the control's (T1's run of the same prompts), because the arithmetic is the served one. THE EVIDENCE: a differing word on a card is the end of the one-launch arm (E0 broken: the argument in docs/sdpa-multi.md has a hole), not a tuning problem.
# The audit adds a launch per layer and the served launches beside it: this arm proves exactness and is never a timed one. Duration (estimate): 120 min. Stop rule: any audit mismatch, refusal, hang or stall stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sdpa-multi eight-seat 262k development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sdpa-multi and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sdpa-multi-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/sdpa-multi commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sdpa-multi-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-sdpamulti-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_code,concurrent8_steady
